From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:03:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] moe: stage mapped experts only, cut unstaged uploads at
 registered edges

The host stager copied every upload of a host expert through its pinned
buffers, also when the experts had been read into an allocated buffer
(no mmap). Nothing faults there and the buffer is pinned when the backend
offers pinned host memory, so the copy only cost time: generation on a
97 GiB expert pool (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, RTX 5090) ran at 36 tok/s against
63 with --moe-stage-mib 0. The stager is now created only when an expert
tensor lives in a mapping (llama_model::is_mapped).

Without the stager, an upload next to a registered range of the RAM tier
(--moe-ram-register-mib) died in the first decode with a CUDA 'invalid
argument': the ranges are page-rounded, so a neighbouring expert shares
its first or last page with one, and the driver refuses a copy that
straddles the edge of a registration. llama_moe_host_registry::upload
cuts unstaged copies at the edges; the cache misses, the seed and the
large batches go through it.
---
